WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:04.800
- [Narrator] Russian
State Media has reported

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:06.750
that jailed Wall Street
Journal correspondent,

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:08.610
Evan Gershkovich has been formally

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:10.170
charged with espionage,

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:11.520
an allegation that The Journal

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:13.920
and the US government vehemently deny.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.410
- The charge of espionage is ridiculous.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.090
- [Narrator] His detention
is the first case

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:19.830
of an American journalist arrested

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.020
by Moscow on allegations of spying

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:23.280
since the Cold War,

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.620
and has prompted a growing
list of individuals,

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:27.690
organizations and government officials

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.140
to call for his release

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:33.300
On March 29th, while on a reporting trip,

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.100
Gershkovich was detained in the city

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.580
of Yekaterinburg around
800 miles east of Moscow

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:41.130
by Russia's main security agency.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:41.963
On March 30th,

00:00:41.963 --> 00:00:43.950
Gershkovich was seen being escorted

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:47.040
into a vehicle after
appearing in a Moscow court.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.080
The press service of the
court said he was ordered

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.570
to be held in custody until May 29th,

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:54.210
according to state news agency TASS.

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:55.897
Russia's Federal Security Bureau said,

00:00:55.897 --> 00:00:58.020
"Gershkovich acting on the instructions

00:00:58.020 --> 00:00:59.160
of the American side,

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.950
collected information
constituting a state secret

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:04.170
about the activities of
one of the enterprises

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:07.290
of the Russian
military-industrial complex."

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:08.137
The Journal said it

00:01:08.137 --> 00:01:11.010
"vehemently denies the
allegations from the FSB

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:13.230
and seeks the immediate
release of our trusted

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:15.810
and dedicated reporter, Evan Gershkovich.

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:19.080
We stand in solidarity
with Evan and his family."

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:21.060
The arrest of the 31 year old reporter

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:23.040
marked the latest diplomatic flashpoint

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.260
between Moscow and Washington.

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:27.120
- The targeting of American citizens

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.150
by Russian government is unacceptable.

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:33.420
We condemn the detention
of Mr. Gershkovich

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:36.660
in the strongest terms.

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:39.360
We also condemn the Russian
government's continued

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:43.143
targeting and repression of journalists.

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:44.970
- [Narrator] On March 31st,

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:46.530
President Biden urged Russia

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:48.439
to release Gershkovich.

00:01:48.439 --> 00:01:49.272
- [Reporter] What's your message

00:01:49.272 --> 00:01:50.713
to Russia right now as
they're detaining the-

00:01:50.713 --> 00:01:52.080
- To who?
- [Reporter] To Russia

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:54.600
as they're detaining The
Wall Street Journal reporter.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:55.650
- Let him go.

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:57.780
We're in process.

00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:59.370
- [Narrator] Gershkovich
was accredited to work

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:00.540
as a journalist in Russia

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:02.070
by the country's foreign ministry

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:04.110
at the time of his detention.

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:06.690
Biden said the US didn't
plan any expulsion

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:09.870
of Russian journalists
or diplomats in response.

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:12.858
- That's not the plan right now.

00:02:12.858 --> 00:02:13.691
- [Narrator] The Wall Street Journal,

00:02:13.691 --> 00:02:15.300
editor in chief, Emma Tucker spoke

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.920
to CNN's Anderson Cooper

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.510
about Gershkovich's detainment

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:19.983
and the charges against him.

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:22.023
- It's utter rubbish.

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:26.340
Evan was doing what reporters do

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:27.420
and what he did very well.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:29.640
He was out there gathering news,

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:31.380
talking to people, reporting,

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:33.270
providing an eyewitness account

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:35.220
of what's going on inside Russia.

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:36.480
- [Narrator] Speaking at a news conference

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:38.820
on April 3rd, NATO Secretary General,

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:41.430
Jens Stoltenberg said Gershkovich's arrest

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:42.870
was of great concern.

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:46.140
- It is important to respect
freedom of the press,

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:49.650
the rights of journalists, and the rights

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:52.800
to ask questions and to do their job.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:56.640
So therefore, we call on
his immediate release.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:57.780
- [Narrator] At the United Nations,

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.370
Russia's ambassador declined

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:02.190
to discuss Gershkovich case in any detail,

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:04.500
citing what he referred
to as the separation

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:06.990
of powers in the Russian justice system.

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:09.300
- Today, Secretary Blinken talked

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:11.973
to Minister Lavrov on that issue.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:16.680
But that will be decided
not by Minister Lavrov

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:20.940
or Secretary Blinken, but by investigation

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:22.050
and by the evidence

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:24.210
that the investigation could provide

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:25.170
for the court.

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:26.700
- Good afternoon, everybody.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:27.533
- [Narrator] On April 4th,

00:03:27.533 --> 00:03:28.770
White House Press secretary,

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:30.210
Karine Jean-Pierre said,

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:32.490
the US will continue
pressing for his release

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:34.950
and seek consular access to him.

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:36.540
- Evan is not a spy.

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:38.010
Evan has never been a spy.

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:40.470
Evan has never worked
for the US government.

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:41.340
- [Narrator] That same day,

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:42.750
Gershkovich's lawyers met with him

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:44.167
in prison and reported that,

00:03:44.167 --> 00:03:46.200
"Evan's Health is good and he is grateful

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.520
for the outpouring of support

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.050
from around the world."

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:51.000
Secretary of State, Antony Blinken said

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.490
on April 5th that the
state department's process

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:55.080
to reach an official wrongfully

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:57.240
detained determination was pending.

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:59.220
- In my own mind, there's no doubt

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:02.220
that he's being wrongfully
detained by Russia

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:03.390
which is exactly what I said

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:04.920
to Foreign Minister Lavrov when I spoke

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:09.030
to him over the weekend and insisted

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:11.823
that Evan be released immediately.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:15.820
But I want to make sure that as always

00:04:16.729 --> 00:04:18.870
because there is a formal process,

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:20.850
that we go through it and we will,

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:24.780
and I expect that to be completed soon.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:26.790
- [Narrator] On April
6th, a Moscow court said

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:27.990
that it would hear an appeal

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:30.840
from Gershkovich's lawyers on April 18th.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:33.600
The court could uphold
his continued detention,

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.580
order him moved to another jail,

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:38.545
allow him house arrest, or grant him bail.

00:04:38.545 --> 00:04:42.128
(gentle suspenseful music)

